  "details": "Summary:\n\nI would like to suggest a feature that allows users to register or \"pin\" their most frequently used camera functions as shortcuts.\n\nThe Problem:\n\nCurrently, the camera menu has a large number of functions and settings lined up in a single row. This often requires significant horizontal scrolling to find the specific tool I need. Furthermore, there are many menu items that I rarely or never use, which clutters the interface and slows down the process of taking photos.\n\nProposed Solution:\n\nAdd a \"Favorites\" or \"Shortcut\" section to the camera UI where users can:\n\n• Pin their most-used functions (e.g., specific filters, focus settings, or mask modes) to the front of the menu.\n\n• Hide or reorder functions that are not relevant to their workflow.\n\nBenefit:\n\nThis would drastically improve the user experience for VRChat photographers. Being able to access preferred settings instantly would make capturing spontaneous moments much smoother and less frustrating.",
